17592186549048 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549048 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $F(x)=x{e}^{3(x-1)}$ for $x\\in [0,5),$ and let $f(x)$ be the **odd** extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in (-5,5).$ What is the value of $f(-1)?$\n\n$f(-1)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549048 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c0b2f698-58d0-5aff-9d1c-cd41dc57daac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549048 #edb/ref 1074 "If $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [0,5),$ the odd extension of $F$ is the function $f$ such that\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}F(x), & x\\in [0,5), \\\\ -F(-x), & x\\in (-5,0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our cases, for $x\\in (-5,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-F(-x) \\\\  & =-(-x){e}^{3(-x-1)} \\\\  & =x{e}^{3(-x-1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & =(-1){e}^{3(-(-1)-1)}=-{e}^{3(0)}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
